(6184842, 911795, 28359, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :-) <br/> <br/>I see you signed up a little while ago and this is your first submission to a challenge. Congrats on taking the plunge. I scored the image a 5 in the challenge, here is why:<br/> <br/>The base technical aspects is not bad. You composition is the strongest part of the image. I think the post processing of the image is the reason why it didn''t score much higher then it did. The exposure is ok, but the lighting is a little flat. It''s lacking contrast and color pop. It meets the challenge description well. I think the best advice I could give you is to study prior challenges that finished in the top 20. It helps to vote in challenges to give you some perspective on how successful images look/feel. We have some great tutorials here, along with the web it self. Keep shooting, reading &amp; learning. It''s fun to see how we start here and in time how we have improved.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :-)  I see you signed up a little while ago and this is your first submission to a challenge. Congrats on taking the plunge. I scored the image a 5 in the challenge, here is why: The base technical aspects is not bad. You composition is the strongest part of the image. I think the post processing of the image is the reason why it didn''t score much higher then it did. The exposure is ok, but the lighting is a little flat. It''s lacking contrast and color pop. It meets the challenge description well. I think the best advice I could give you is to study prior challenges that finished in the top 20. It helps to vote in challenges to give you some perspective on how successful images look/feel. We have some great tutorials here, along with the web it self. Keep shooting, reading & learning. It''s fun to see how we start here and in time how we have improved.', '2010-10-07 15:59:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(6184942, 911427, 113419, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>First Impressions: <br/>What a beautiful photograph!  That''s totally it - my first impression!<br/> <br/>Technical (Comp, lighting, color, focus): <br/>clear sharp focus, perfect time of day for the lighting in this photo, outstanding colors,  the only thing I see wrong in the composition is really just nit-picky stuff which could be quickly taken care of in the slightest of crops on the left hand (looking at image) side....as I said in an earlier comment to remove that gravel(?) on the bottom left which would also take care of the wire that someone else caught and mentioned in another comment.<br/> <br/>Challenge: <br/>Don''t think you can get much more country than what you''ve captured.<br/> <br/>Artistic/Emotion: <br/>Artisticly this is simply stunning.<br/>Emotionally it makes me wanna walk down the slope and get to work!<br/> <br/>Summary: <br/>It''s in the top 10!  That pretty much sums it all up!  ;-)<br/>This is indeed a wonderful entry.  Thank you for sharing it with us.  :-)<br/> <br/>edited to fix the tag  ;-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-10-08 12:28:36.</i></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  First Impressions: What a beautiful photograph!  That''s totally it - my first impression! Technical (Comp, lighting, color, focus): clear sharp focus, perfect time of day for the lighting in this photo, outstanding colors,  the only thing I see wrong in the composition is really just nit-picky stuff which could be quickly taken care of in the slightest of crops on the left hand (looking at image) side....as I said in an earlier comment to remove that gravel(?) on the bottom left which would also take care of the wire that someone else caught and mentioned in another comment. Challenge: Don''t think you can get much more country than what you''ve captured. Artistic/Emotion: Artisticly this is simply stunning.Emotionally it makes me wanna walk down the slope and get to work! Summary: It''s in the top 10!  That pretty much sums it all up!  ;-)This is indeed a wonderful entry.  Thank you for sharing it with us.  :-) edited to fix the tag  ;-)', '2010-10-07 17:26:52.000000', '2010-10-08 13:28:36.000000', 0),
